WEBVTT

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:06.650
Morning, Nagi!

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:07.980
Morning.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:12.200
It's gotten cold all of a sudden.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.320
Well, it's almost the end of October, after all.

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:16.990
Oh, Halloween.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.160
Oh yeah!

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:22.790
Come to think of it, Halloween decorations are starting to show up everywhere.

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:24.040
Yeah, they are.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.750
It feels like it's become a tradition in Japan now, too.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.840
No kidding.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:31.840
Aren't you scared?

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.590
Hm? Er... huh?

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:37.600
Nagi?

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.640
You can't have Halloween without ghosts.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.730
Isn't it scary?

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.310
No, not really.

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:51.440
I mean, Halloween ghosts aren't real ones.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:55.240
I'm just a little uncomfortable with scary stories.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:57.320
Just a little, eh?

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.120
Just a little!

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:04.080
Nagi, I'll bet there are things you're uncomfortable with, too.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.120
No, I can't think of anything.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:08.380
Good morning!

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:11.710
Okay! Put some spirit in it!

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:13.760
Good morning...

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:15.800
Okay! Good morning!

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.100
Good morning!

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:21.310
I thought you weren't uncomfortable with anything?

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:26.230
Let's give it 110% today!

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:30.110
Well... I'm uncomfortable with that too.

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:31.980
Good morning!

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:10.750
Ah, Nagi-chan, Yuuko-chan! Morning!

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.630
Morning...

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:16.460
Huh? You two seem worn out. What happened?

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.630
First thing in the morning...

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:20.630
hot-blooded.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:21.970
Nagi-chan?

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:25.140
Everyone has things they're uncomfortable with.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:26.680
What?

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:27.470
Whoa!

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:30.180
What's this?!

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:32.850
What is it?

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.690
There's a strange doll on my desk...

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:38.610
Ugh! It's so creepy!

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:39.240
Right?

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:42.490
Ah, maybe it has to do with Halloween?

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:44.740
You know, "Trick-or-Treat"!

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:47.290
A trick? Is someone harassing me?

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:49.790
It sounds likely, that's for sure.

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.040
Should you throw it away?

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:54.540
But I might get cursed if I do.

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:58.460
<i>What do I do? I can't admit that I made it.</i>

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:02.680
What? You made that doll, Run?

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:04.890
I-I'm so sorry I said those mean things!

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:06.600
Oh, no, it's okay.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:11.390
You said you liked them, so I did my best to make one,

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:14.150
but animals are hard.

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:15.610
It doesn't look like one, does it?

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:17.870
No, no, you did great!

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:19.110
Yeah, yeah!

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:20.280
Especially these...

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:22.780
ear-like things...

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:24.820
no, horns?

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:29.830
I like the glaring- I mean, soulfully gazing eyes...

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:35.330
Right, the mouth! The way it's gaping open is really distinctive!

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:38.590
Right, right! It looks exactly like one!

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:42.920
<i>Actually... this thing I'm supposed to like...</i>

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.090
<i>what exactly is it?</i>

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:46.970
Does it look like one?

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:48.430
Yeah...

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:51.430
A Halloween party?

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:53.350
How did that come up?

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.650
Well, after an incident this morning, we got on the topic.

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:59.650
I've been interested in Halloween for a while now!

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:03.400
Plus, tomorrow's Saturday. Let's all make some sweets and eat them!

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.030
I can't wait!

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.370
What kind of sweets should we make?

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:10.280
Cookies or something? Or maybe cake?

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:11.910
I'll pass.

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:15.540
Nagi-chan, you don't like making sweets?

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:18.460
Cooking involves all those precise measurements.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:20.460
It's not really my thing.

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:23.920
Also, well, I'm on a diet.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.880
It'll be fine!

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:29.930
I'll count the calories carefully, just for you.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.350
Would you really?

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:32.680
Of course!

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:34.600
Well, if I'm just eating them.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:35.310
That's more like it!

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:37.020
What about you, Tooru?

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:40.860
I'll probably be a bit late.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.320
I see.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:44.990
When you're finished, I'll go to your house to eat them.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:46.200
All right then!

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:50.120
Then I'll go with Tooru.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:51.030
Got it!

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:54.700
In that case, do you want to help me cook, Yuuko-chan?

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:58.250
No problem. Is there anything I should bring?

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:01.340
Hmm. My mom likes to cook sweets,

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:03.460
so we should have everything we need.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:05.880
I see. I'm looking forward to this!

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:08.550
All right! Let's do our best tomorrow!

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:09.720
Yeah!

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.440
Run, what are you drawing?

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:33.620
This! It's word chain pictionary for the exchange diary I'm doing with Tooru!

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:38.460
What does it look like?

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:42.460
<i>A repeat of that doll incident?</i>

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:52.760
<i>For starters, is it an animal?</i>

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:55.390
<i>Well, it sort of resembles a bug...</i>

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:57.770
Is it too tricky?

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:00.900
Then here's a hint:

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:02.310
people often eat them.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:05.980
<i>Wha... it's edible?</i>

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:08.530
That was a huge hint.

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:10.320
It's a zebra, isn't it?

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:12.530
Bullseye, Tooru!

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:14.330
<i>Z-</i>

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:16.540
<i>Zebra?</i>

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:18.450
Smart as always, Tooru!

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:21.000
<i>Th-That's a zebra?</i>

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.130
<i>Am I just thick?</i>

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:25.800
Nagi, you're overthinking it.

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:36.060
I'm happy she gave it to me, but it's kind of scary.

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:38.680
Nagi, you're not leaving yet?

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.480
No, I was about to.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:45.310
By the way, want to meet up before we go to Run-chan's tomorrow?

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:47.940
Hmm... yeah, that'd be more convenient.

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:49.940
Then how about the North entrance to the station?

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:51.990
It's near the entrance to the shopping district.

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:52.490
Got it.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:58.330
T-Tooru! Th-That thing!

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.330
This?

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:02.920
Run-chan gave it to me.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.000
W-Well, I figured as much.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.040
Then what?

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:11.380
What's that a doll of?

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:17.760
Oh? You can't tell, Nagi?

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:23.190
<i>For some reason, this really bugs me.</i>

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:27.730
Actually, she gave me something similar...

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:29.570
It's big!

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:34.740
No fair.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:40.290
Please, if you would be so kind, allow me to have it.

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:43.790
Huh? Why, I couldn't possibly. It belongs to me.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.670
Don't say that-

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:48.340
No fair!

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:50.210
Why, it's perfectly fair.

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:51.510
We're here!

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:54.260
Let's head home!

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:56.470
I need to get ready, so wait up.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:58.800
Sure. Make it quick.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:02.890
By the way, Nagi.

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:03.480
Hm?

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:06.440
What's your favorite animal?

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:09.980
Don't tell me you're going to use it for word chain pictionary.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:11.480
No, that's not it.

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:13.360
I was just curious.

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:15.490
I see.

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:17.910
Let me think.

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:20.490
I like small animals. They're cute.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:22.330
Like squirrels!

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:24.410
Ah, squirrels are cute, aren't they?

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:27.500
On that note, this.

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:30.090
I didn't say what it was, now did I?

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:31.500
Huh?

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:33.710
We're ready!

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:36.510
Come on now, tell me!

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:38.430
Squirrels are cute, aren't they?

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:39.930
Hey, Tooru!

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:41.350
Small animals...

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:43.350
Tell me!

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:47.210
I'm home!

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:05.580
Yep. Still scary.

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:22.430
Over here?

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:25.060
Trick-or-Treat!

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:26.600
Here you go.

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:27.310
Thank you!

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:30.650
<i>Looks like all the stores are decked out in Halloween colors.</i>

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:32.190
<i>Now,</i>

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:35.070
<i>we were supposed to meet around here...</i>

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:38.070
I said, "Trick-or-Treat!"

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:40.740
Oh. Nagi.

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:42.870
Hand it over!

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:48.040
I kept saying I didn't work here, but the little brats...

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:50.960
I'm not even carrying any candy...

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:51.420
Whoa...

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:57.800
Tooru, are those supposed to be your casual clothes?

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:02.430
Huh?

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:06.720
Do we usually pass through this shopping district on the way to Run's?

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:07.640
Never been here?

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:08.730
Nope.

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:12.440
If I recall, we went a different way the last time we went to Run's.

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:16.320
Precisely. This is a slight detour.

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:17.690
You know.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:22.410
Run-chan said she's making sweets, so we need replacement sweets.

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:24.950
Oh, so we're here to buy those.

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:26.990
Wait, so it's a given she'll mess up?

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:29.290
Oh, Tooru-chan!

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.120
Good afternoon.

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:33.380
You're looking well.

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:36.090
Here.

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:37.500
Take this.

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:41.840
Thank you.

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:45.930
Tooru-chan!

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:46.470
Huh?

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:49.480
Here, have it! It's good!

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:51.480
Go on, take it!

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:52.690
Thank you, ma'am.

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:54.730
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:59.030
<i>Tooru mentioned during the festival that people in the shopping district give her stuff.</i>

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:01.110
Tooru-chan! Here, take this!

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:02.660
My, you've come to visit.

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:04.660
Here, use this, Tooru.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:07.660
<i>In fact, she's not paying for anything!</i>

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:11.410
What's this all of a sudden?

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:14.500
We still have time, so we're stopping by this bookstore.

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:15.330
I see.

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:19.590
Actually, that's perfect. There's a book I want, too.

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:32.180
Hey, Tooru, isn't this-

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:47.160
Nagi...

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:35.040
In this manga...

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:35.790
Hm?

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:38.500
This Yoshinoko looks like Yuuko.

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:40.750
Hey, isn't that an ero-manga?

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:46.550
Wow, you're right. She totally looks the same.

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:48.590
Just look at this. It's a short story collection,

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:52.260
but all the heroines have the same face.

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:04.280
If we showed the author a photo of Yuuko,

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:05.610
he'd probably pay good money for it.

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:07.780
Let's buy this book.

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:10.240
Okay, let's get started!

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:12.620
Yuuko-chan, do you want an apron?

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:13.660
Sure, I'll take it.

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:18.000
Your mom must be really into making sweets.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:20.670
Oh, look at all the cute cookie-cutters!

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:24.460
Hey, are we allowed to use all the stuff here?

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:27.420
Yeah. She said to use whatever we want.

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:30.050
Really? I'm so excited!

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:32.300
So, what are we making them with?

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:34.390
Uh, hang on a sec.

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:36.180
Here we go...

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:39.440
This!

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:41.360
Hotcakes!

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:43.820
Huh?

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:46.740
For Halloween?

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:50.030
Yep. I felt like hotcakes today!

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:51.870
R-Really?

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:59.120
Oh yeah! The other day, I cracked an egg with one hand!

00:14:59.120 --> 00:14:59.960
Really?

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:00.620
Watch me!

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:34.200
The other day, I cracked an egg with one hand...

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:40.290
Run, let's just move on...

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:43.630
I guess that does it.

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:44.920
Yep. This should be fine.

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:47.920
I'll put it on the griddle, then.

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:48.630
Okay.

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:53.300
Run!

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:09.070
Thank good...

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:10.190
ness!

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:17.200
Ow...

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:28.460
I'm sorry, I'm sorry! I'll redo it!

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:30.920
I-It's okay! Don't rush!

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:35.180
It was my clumsy mistake, so why did Yuuko-chan have to suffer?

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:38.060
Oh, come on, don't worry about it!

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:39.890
I know!

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:42.180
I should suffer instead!

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:42.770
Huh?

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:44.850
Yah!

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:46.940
Whaaaaaat?!

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:49.980
What do we do?

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:52.240
Take a bath?

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:53.700
'Kay.

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:01.080
Yuuko-chan!

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:01.370
Hm?

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:04.920
Your figure's so nice, Yuuko-chan.

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:06.670
Aw, that's not true.

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:08.460
Is it because of your pets?

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:09.500
Huh?

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:13.590
What was it again? Uh, sounded like an office supply...

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:14.220
Oh yeah!

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:16.090
Tapeworms!

00:17:16.090 --> 00:17:17.260
That again?

00:17:17.260 --> 00:17:19.220
You use the power of the tapeworms!

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:21.890
Like I said, they're not pets, and I don't have any!

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:36.740
Wearing this, in someone else's house...

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:41.540
I'll leave your change of clothes in the living room, 'kay?

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:45.790
I should have asked her to bring it when we got in the bath.

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:49.290
Dynamite!

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:51.300
Y-You were here?

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:53.880
Such immodesty, and in someone else's house!

00:17:53.880 --> 00:17:56.550
I don't recall raising such an indecent daughter as you!

00:17:56.970 --> 00:17:58.340
Eh? Wh-What?

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:00.140
What are you saying?

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:02.220
How dare you speak to me like that, father?

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:05.850
Huh? What? Nagi, what's going on here?

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:10.060
We've been practicing for your sake, so listen up!

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:11.020
Practicing what?

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:15.570
What is that manga?

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:19.450
We found a sexy manga starring your lookalike.

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:22.450
What? No! A perverted manga?

00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:25.120
Here, take a look!

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:29.170
No, stop it! I hate perverted stuff!

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:31.590
Geez!

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:35.960
What is this? Oh no...

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:41.010
So she says, but she'll read the whole thing at this rate.

00:18:41.010 --> 00:18:42.890
Yuuko-chan, what's wrong?

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:44.100
Hey-

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:47.730
What's wrong, Tooru?

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:49.390
Not for you, Run-chan.

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:51.860
Well, I'm glad you like it.

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:52.860
Huh?

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:56.570
Wow! Look at all the snacks!

00:18:57.110 --> 00:19:00.360
Tooru got these all for free at the shopping district.

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:02.370
That's amazing, Tooru!

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:03.530
But what a relief!

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:07.950
I was hoping we could all eat hotcakes...

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:11.630
<i>Run-chan's hotcakes...</i>

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:13.380
but we screwed up.

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:15.130
Don't sweat it.

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:20.220
Okay. But I still wish we could have had hotcakes.

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:21.890
Just make them next time.

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:24.430
Yeah, I guess you're right.

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:27.430
Well, shall we get started?

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:29.230
All right, let's have a toast!

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:33.980
Since it's Halloween, should we toast the ghosts?

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:36.940
Maybe we should. Or how about <i>no!</i>

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:39.740
Wait a sec.

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:40.860
Huh?

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:44.740
Let's make some now!

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:46.620
Huh?

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:51.330
Make it again? But we're out of hotcake mix.

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:52.620
Don't worry!

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:56.340
There it is!

00:19:57.380 --> 00:19:58.630
We can make them with this!

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:04.220
Are you ready?

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:05.050
Yeah.

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:16.500
Here, Yuuko. Say "ahh".

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:17.830
Gosh, stop that!

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:28.220
Ah, I'm stuffed!

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:30.810
Nagi, what about your diet?

00:21:30.810 --> 00:21:34.180
Wha- I thought you were counting the calories!

00:21:34.180 --> 00:21:37.520
Don't worry. I made the recipe less sweet.

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:39.980
Come on, don't scare me.

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:42.150
Tooru.

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:44.650
We'll clean up together.

00:21:44.650 --> 00:21:45.360
'Kay.

00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:46.910
Come to think of it, your outfit, Tooru.

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:49.280
It looks like cosplay. It's so cute!

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:51.080
Oh...

00:21:51.580 --> 00:21:54.450
Thanks to those clothes, the kids were all over her.

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:57.210
Really? How nice, Tooru!

00:21:57.210 --> 00:22:00.630
Nah, they were tugging at her clothes and crying at her...

00:22:00.630 --> 00:22:04.050
Maybe you should have handed out candy, like last year?

00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:05.880
Huh?

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:09.800
Tooru likes kids, so last year-

00:22:09.800 --> 00:22:11.760
You don't have to tell them that.

00:22:11.760 --> 00:22:13.390
What's wrong, Tooru?

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:19.860
Tooru, totally unexpected!

00:22:19.860 --> 00:22:20.690
You've got it wrong!

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:22.400
Tooru loves kids!

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:24.230
You've got it wrong!

00:23:57.240 --> 00:23:59.740
What's up with this subtitle?

00:23:59.740 --> 00:24:01.330
Um... A beverage?

00:24:01.330 --> 00:24:04.000
Isn't it sad to act like you don't know even though you do?

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:07.120
Shut up. This is a promise!

00:24:07.120 --> 00:24:12.960
Yutaka, I wonder if it's about time we put your name in the subtitle?

00:24:12.960 --> 00:24:16.260
I think we'd be finished talking in no time, if so.

00:24:16.260 --> 00:24:18.930
Next time on A Channel: Carbonic Acid.

00:24:18.930 --> 00:24:20.410
Okay then, how about "Yutaka and Toorun"-

00:24:20.410 --> 00:24:24.060
Hey, I'm here, so let's make it the three of us!
